ission or higher, is not the App, and comes after the last triage `:done` label of the issue. An approval given earlier is left in place and ignored: the gate waits for a fresh one and does not escalate. An approval from anyone else adds `ard:needs-human` with a comment that does not name the actor. A human who adds `ard:worker:<role>` directly bypasses the gate and has approved by doing so. The gate does not enforce that `triage:engineer` ran: the lead routes and the gate applies its routing. In `--dry-run` the gate logs `triage.would_gate` and writes nothing; otherwise each action records a `gate` event.\n+Before it asks for approval or starts a worker, the gate checks that `.ard/<n>/plan.md` exists on `main`. If it does not, the gate posts one comment, adds `ard:needs-human` and records a `gate` event with reason `no-plan`; a check that fails to run is retried on the next tick. Removing a role's request label by hand does not count as that role finishing. With `require_approval: true` (the Phase 1 default) the gate posts one \"ready for approval\" comment per lead job and waits. `ard:approved` is honoured only when its latest `labeled` event (reset by an `unlabeled`) is by a collaborator with triage permission or higher, is not the App, and comes after the last triage `:done` label of the issue. An approval given earlier is left in place and ignored: the gate waits for a fresh one and does not escalate. An approval from anyone else adds `ard:needs-human` with a comment that does not name the actor. In `ard serve`'s terminal UI the `a` key on a queued issue asks for confirmation, then runs the operator's own `gh issue edit --add-label ard:approved` (or opens the issue URL when `gh` is missing or logged out) and wakes the triage loop; the App never adds `ard:approved`, and under `--dry-run` the call is recorded in the ledger, not run. A human who adds `ard:worker:<role>` directly bypasses the gate and has approved by doing so. The gate does not enforce that `triage:engineer` ran: the lead routes and the gate applies its routing. In `--dry-run` the gate logs `triage.would_gate` and writes nothing; otherwise each action records a `gate` event.\n \n **Order comes from config, not the lead.** A role can declare `after: [architect, product-manager]`; the controller holds its request until those roles, if requested, are done. A prerequisite is requested when its request label (`ard:pending` for the lead) or its `:running` label is present, and done when its `:done` label is present; one that was never requested does not hold. A held role is logged as `triage.held`, is not a candidate and does not count against the one-triage-job-per-issue rule. Config rejects a role that is after itself and any cycle. Engineer triage normally runs last so its steps reflect the design and requirements.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/effects/approve.go b/internal/effects/approve.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..262e332\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/effects/approve.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+package effects\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strconv\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/repopath\"\n+)\n+\n+// ErrGHUnavailable is returned by ApproveIssue when the gh CLI is not on PATH\n+// or is not logged in. Callers fall back to showing the issue URL.\n+var ErrGHUnavailable = errors.New(\"effects: gh is missing or not logged in\")\n+\n+// ghPath finds the gh binary. A variable for tests.\n+var ghPath = exec.LookPath\n+\n+// ApproveIssue adds ard:approved through the operator's own gh, so the label\n+// event carries the operator's identity and the gate checks their permission.\n+// ard never reads the operator's token, and the GitHub App client is not used.\n+func (l *Live) ApproveIssue(ctx context.Context, repo string, n int) error {\n+\tif err := bad(\"ApproveIssue\", n); err != nil {\n+\t\treturn err\n+\t}\n+\tif _, _, err := repopath.Parts(repo); err != nil {\n+\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, err, \"repo\", repo)\n+\t}\n+\tpath, err := ghPath(\"gh\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, ErrGHUnavailable, \"repo\", repo)\n+\t}\n+\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, path, \"issue\", \"edit\", strconv.Itoa(n), \"--add-label\", labels.Approved, \"-R\", repo)\n+\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n+\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n+\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n+\t\tmsg := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n+\t\tlow := strings.ToLower(msg)\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(low, \"gh auth login\") || strings.Contains(low, \"not logged in\") || strings.Contains(low, \"authentication\") {\n+\t\t\terr = ErrGHUnavailable\n+\t\t} else {\n+\t\t\tif len(msg) > 300 {\n+\t\t\t\tmsg = msg[:300]\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\terr = fmt.Errorf(\"gh issue edit: %w: %s\", err, msg)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, err, \"repo\", repo)\n+\t}\n+\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, nil, \"repo\", repo)\n+}\n+\n+// ApproveIssue records the call and runs nothing.\n+func (d *DryRun) ApproveIssue(ctx context.Context, repo string, n int) error {\n+\t_, err := d.emit(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", repo, map[string]any{\"issue\": n, \"label\": labels.Approved}, false, nil)\n+\treturn err\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/effects/approve_test.go b/internal/effects/approve_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9a77118\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/effects/approve_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@\n+package effects\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"log/slog\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github/fake\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n+)\n+\n+// fakeGH puts a gh script on PATH that records argv to a file and exits with\n+// code after printing stderr. It returns the argv file's path.\n+func fakeGH(t *testing.T, code int, stderr string) string {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tdir := t.TempDir()\n+\targv := filepath.Join(dir, \"argv\")\n+\tscript := \"#!/bin/sh\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' \\\"$*\\\" >> '\" + argv + \"'\\nprintf '%s' '\" + stderr + \"' >&2\\nexit \" + string(rune('0'+code)) + \"\\n\"\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, \"gh\"), []byte(script), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tt.Setenv(\"PATH\", dir)\n+\treturn argv\n+}\n+\n+func newLiveT(t *testing.T) *Live {\n+\treturn NewLive(failClient{Reader: fake.New(), t: t}, gitx.New(\"\"), slog.New(slog.DiscardHandler))\n+}\n+\n+func TestApproveIssueRunsGH(t *testing.T) {\n+\targv := fakeGH(t, 0, \"\")\n+\tif err := newLiveT(t).ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 42); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tb, _ := os.ReadFile(argv)\n+\tif got, want := strings.TrimSpace(string(b)), \"issue edit 42 --add-label ard:approved -R o/r\"; got != want {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"argv = %q, want %q\", got, want)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestApproveIssueNoGH(t *testing.T) {\n+\tt.Setenv(\"PATH\", t.TempDir())\n+\tif err := newLiveT(t).ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 42); !errors.Is(err, ErrGHUnavailable) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestApproveIssueNotLoggedIn(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfakeGH(t, 1, \"To get started with GitHub CLI, please run:  gh auth login\")\n+\tif err := newLiveT(t).ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 42); !errors.Is(err, ErrGHUnavailable) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestApproveIssueOtherFailure(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfakeGH(t, 1, \"boom\")\n+\terr := newLiveT(t).ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 42)\n+\tif err == nil || errors.Is(err, ErrGHUnavailable) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestApproveIssueBadInput(t *testing.T) {\n+\targv := fakeGH(t, 0, \"\")\n+\tl := newLiveT(t)\n+\tfor _, c := range []struct {\n+\t\trepo string\n+\t\tn    int\n+\t}{{\"o/r\", 0}, {\"o/r\", -1}, {\"o/r;rm\", 5}, {\"o\", 5}, {\"\", 5}} {\n+\t\tif err := l.ApproveIssue(context.Background(), c.repo, c.n); err == nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%+v: no error\", c)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Stat(argv); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"gh ran on bad input\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// The App client must never be touched: failClient fails the test on any write.\n+func TestApproveNeverUsesAppClient(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfakeGH(t, 0, \"\")\n+\tif err := newLiveT(t).ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 7); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestDryRunApproveRecords(t *testing.T) {\n+\targv := fakeGH(t, 0, \"\")\n+\tled := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"ledger.jsonl\")\n+\td, err := NewDryRun(DryRunOptions{Log: slog.New(slog.DiscardHandler), LedgerPath: led})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer d.Close()\n+\tif err := d.ApproveIssue(context.Background(), \"o/r\", 42); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tb, _ := os.ReadFile(led)\n+\tif !strings.Contains(string(b), `\"op\":\"ApproveIssue\"`) || !strings.Contains(string(b), \"ard:approved\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ledger = %s\", b)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Stat(argv); err == nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"gh ran in dry-run\")\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/effects/effects.go b/internal/effects/effects.go\nindex 947f441..e7eb42f 100644\n--- a/internal/effects/effects.go\n+++ b/internal/effects/effects.go\n@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@ type Effects interface {\n \t// ErrNothingToCommit when nothing is staged.\n \tCommit(ctx context.Context, op CommitOp) (CommitResult, error)\n \tPush(ctx context.Context, op PushOp) error\n+\t// ApproveIssue runs the operator's own gh to add ard:approved to issue n\n+\t// of repo (owner/name). It is not part of github.Writer, so the App client\n+\t// can never reach it. ErrGHUnavailable means gh is missing or logged out.\n+\tApproveIssue(ctx context.Context, repo string, n int) error\n \t// DryRun reports whether effects are only logged.\n \tDryRun() bool\n }\ndiff --git a/internal/servecmd/approve.go b/internal/servecmd/approve.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b