only inside effects).\n4. `internal/snapshot/snapshot.go` (edit): new type `QueueItem{Issue int; Title, Role, PlanURL string}` and field `Snapshot.Queue []QueueItem` (new). The snapshot must not call GitHub, so fill it from a new in-memory source `Sources.Approvals` (new interface `Queue() []QueueItem`). If #407/#414 already defined a queue field in IssueView, use that instead and skip this step. Titles are stored raw here; the UI sanitises.\n5. `internal/triage/fanin.go` (edit): in `askApproval` (line ~451) record the issue in the queue (number, title from the `github.Issue` that `approved` already has, worker role, plan link `https://github.com/<repo>/blob/main/.ard/<n>/plan.md`). Remove it when `approved` returns true, the label is present, or the issue closes or gets `ard:needs-human`. Guard with a mutex. Keep it a small new type `triage.ApprovalQueue` (new, in `internal/triage/queue.go`) with `Add`, `Remove`, `Snapshot`; wire it in `internal/servecmd/serve.go` and `internal/servecmd/snapshot.go` beside the existing snapshot Sources.\n6. `internal/ui/model.go` and `internal/ui/keys.go` (edit): `New` gets an `approve func(n int) error` field (via a new option or an extra parameter; update `internal/servecmd/ui.go` and the tests' callers). Add `confirmApprove *snapshot.QueueItem` state. In `handleKey`, `a` acts only when the selected issue number is in `m.snap.Queue`; otherwise it is ignored. While the confirm screen is open: `y` runs approve and closes it; Esc, `n`, Enter and every other key cancel (default No). Ctrl-C still quits. Add `a approve` to the help text.\n7. `internal/ui/view.go` and `internal/ui/sanitize.go` (edit): render the confirm screen with number, title, worker role and plan link, all through the existing sanitiser, showing \"Approve? [y/N]\". Show the result line (\"approved #N\", or an error) in the footer.\n8. `internal/servecmd/ui.go` (edit) and `internal/servecmd/approve.go` (new): `approveFn(w *wiring, repo)` calls `Effects.ApproveIssue`. On success it calls `w.wakeLoops(\"ui-approve\", \"triage\")` (the triage loop name is \"triage\"; see `internal/servecmd/loops_test.go`). On `ErrGHUnavailable` it shows `ui.IssueURL(repo, n)` in the status line and calls `ui.OpenBrowser`. Pass this to `ui.New`; `runWithUI` gets the new parameter.\n9. `docs/proposal.md` (edit): add one sentence to the approval paragraph (the one with \"ready for approval\", ~line 287) saying that `ard serve`'s `a` key runs the operator's own `gh issue edit` (or opens the issue URL when gh is missing), that the App never adds `ard:approved`, and that dry-run records the effect. `internal/docscheck` runs in `make lint test`, so run it and keep its conventions.\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `make lint test` (workers/engineer override in .ard/config.yaml).\n- `internal/effects/approve_test.go`: `TestApproveIssueRunsGH` puts a fake `gh` script on PATH (via `t.Setenv(\"PATH\", dir)`) that records argv. Expect exactly `issue edit 42 --add-label ard:approved -R o/r`. `TestApproveIssueNoGH` with an empty PATH returns `ErrGHUnavailable`. `TestApproveIssueBadInput`: n=0, n=-1 and repo `o/r;rm` return an error and run nothing. `TestDryRunApproveRecords`: the ledger holds an `ApproveIssue` record, the fake gh was never run, and no client write was called. `TestApproveNeverUsesAppClient`: with `failClient` (see effects_test.go:32) as the client, `Live.ApproveIssue` makes no client call.\n- `internal/ui/ui_test.go`: `a` on a queue row opens the confirm screen (golden file in `internal/ui/testdata`); `y` calls approve once with the number; Esc, Enter, `n` and a random key call it zero times; `a` on a non-queue row and on an empty list does nothing; a hostile title (ANSI escapes, newline) renders sanitised.\n- `internal/servecmd`: approve success wakes triage once (use a fake controller or wake hook); `ErrGHUnavailable` calls the fake opener with the issue URL; dry-run wake is harmless.\n- `internal/triage`: `askApproval` adds the issue to the queue and `approved` removes it; a repeat does not duplicate it.\n- `internal/snapshot`: the import test must still pass (no `internal/github` import); `Queue` is filled from the source.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. The change spawns a subprocess with the operator's credentials, so arguments must come only from the integer issue number, the constant label and the validated repo. It touches the `Effects` interface (every implementation and fake must compile) and adds shared state between the triage loop and the UI (mutex). No file under `merge.protected_paths` is touched (`docs/proposal.md` and `internal/` are not listed). There are no migrations. Approval is still enforced by the existing gate (actor permission, after the triage `:done`), so a UI approval cannot bypass it.\n\n### Size\nL (about 500 to 800 changed lines, mostly tests and golden files). Files: `internal/effects/{effects,live,dryrun,approve,approve_test}.go`, `internal/snapshot/snapshot.go`, `internal/triage/{fanin,queue}.go`, `internal/ui/{model,keys,view,sanitize,ui_test}.go` plus testdata, `internal/servecmd/{ui,approve,serve,snapshot}.go`, `docs/proposal.md`.\npackage effects\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/repopath\"\n)\n\n// ErrGHUnavailable is returned by ApproveIssue when the gh CLI is not on PATH\n// or is not logged in. Callers fall back to showing the issue URL.\nvar ErrGHUnavailable = errors.New(\"effects: gh is missing or not logged in\")\n\n// ghPath finds the gh binary. A variable for tests.\nvar ghPath = exec.LookPath\n\n// ApproveIssue adds ard:approved through the operator's own gh, so the label\n// event carries the operator's identity and the gate checks their permission.\n// ard never reads the operator's token, and the GitHub App client is not used.\nfunc (l *Live) ApproveIssue(ctx context.Context, repo string, n int) error {\n\tif err := bad(\"ApproveIssue\", n); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif _, _, err := repopath.Parts(repo); err != nil {\n\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, err, \"repo\", repo)\n\t}\n\tpath, err := ghPath(\"gh\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, ErrGHUnavailable, \"repo\", repo)\n\t}\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, path, \"issue\", \"edit\", strconv.Itoa(n), \"--add-label\", labels.Approved, \"-R\", repo)\n\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n\t\tmsg := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\t\tlow := strings.ToLower(msg)\n\t\tif strings.Contains(low, \"gh auth login\") || strings.Contains(low, \"not logged in\") || strings.Contains(low, \"authentication\") {\n\t\t\terr = ErrGHUnavailable\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tif len(msg) > 300 {\n\t\t\t\tmsg = msg[:300]\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\terr = fmt.Errorf(\"gh issue edit: %w: %s\", err, msg)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, err, \"repo\", repo)\n\t}\n\treturn l.done(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", n, nil, \"repo\", repo)\n}\n\n// ApproveIssue records the call and runs nothing.\nfunc (d *DryRun) ApproveIssue(ctx context.Context, repo string, n int) error {\n\t_, err := d.emit(ctx, \"ApproveIssue\", repo, map[string]any{\"issue\": n, \"label\": labels.Approved}, false, nil)\n\treturn err\n}\npackage servecmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/effects\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/ui\"\n)\n\n// approveTimeout bounds one gh call so a hung gh cannot freeze the UI.\nconst approveTimeout = 30 * time.Second\n\n// approveFn returns the UI's approve action. It runs the operator's own gh\n// through the effect layer (dry-run records it instead). On success it wakes\n// the triage loop so the gate runs now. When gh is missing or logged out it\n// opens the issue page instead. The returned string is the status line.\nfunc approveFn(fx effects.Effects, wake func(reason string, names ...string), repo string, open func(string) error) func(n int) (string, error) {\n\treturn func(n int) (string, error) {\n\t\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), approveTimeout)\n\t\tdefer cancel()\n\t\terr := fx.ApproveIssue(ctx, repo, n)\n\t\tswitch {\n\t\tcase err == nil:\n\t\t\twake(\"ui-approve\", \"triage\")\n\t\t\tif fx.DryRun() {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"dry-run: would approve #%d\", n), nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"approved #%d\", n), nil\n\t\tcase errors.Is(err, effects.ErrGHUnavailable):\n\t\t\turl := ui.IssueURL(repo, n)\n\t\t\tif open != nil {\n\t\t\t\t_ = open(url)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"gh unavailable; add ard:approved at %s\", url), nil\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\ndiff --git a/internal/triage/fanin.go b/internal/triage/fanin.go\nindex 14449d2..ba6570e 100644\n--- a/internal/triage/fanin.go\n+++ b/internal/triage/fanin.go\n@@ -213,11 +213,13 @@ func (t *tick) gateIssue(ctx context.Context, n int, busy bool) error {\n \tis, err := l.d.Reader.GetIssue(ctx, n)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\tif errors.Is(err, github.ErrNotFound) {\n+\t\t\tl.d.Approvals.Remove(n)\n \t\t\treturn nil\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"triage gate issue %d: re-read: %w\", n, err)\n \t}\n-\tif is.State != github.StateOpen || is.IsPR {\n+\tif is.State != github.StateOpen || is.IsPR || hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.NeedsHuman) {\n+\t\tl.d.Approvals.Remove(n)\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\n \tworker, jobID, ok, err := closeout.LeadWorker(ctx, l.d.Store, n)\n@@ -378,6 +380,7 @@ func (t *tick) approved(ctx context.Context, is github.Issue, jobID, worker stri\n \tl := t.l\n \tn := is.Number\n \tif !hasLabel(is.Labels, labels.Approved) {\n+\t\tt.queueApproval(is, worker)\n \t\treturn false, t.askApproval(ctx, n, jobID, worker, rounds)\n \t}\n \ttl, err := l.d.Reader.ListTimeline(ctx, n)\n@@ -431,8 +434,10 @@ func (t *tick) approved(ctx context.Context, is github.Issue, jobID, worker stri\n \t}\n \tif !ev.CreatedAt.After(doneAt) {\n \t\tt.log.Info(\"triage.approval_stale\", \"issue\", n)\n+\t\tt.queueApproval(is, worker)\n \t\treturn false, t.askApproval(ctx, n, jobID, worker, rounds)\n \t}\n+\tl.d.Approvals.Remove(n)\n \treturn true, nil\n }\n \n@@ -446,6 +451,12 @@ func (t *tick) gateEvent(ctx context.Context, issue int, verdict, reason, worker\n \t}\n }\n \n+// queueApproval lists the issue for the command center's approve key.\n+func (t *tick) queueApproval(is github.Issue, worker string) {\n+\tt.l.d.Approvals.Add(QueueItem{Issue: is.Number, Title: is.Title, Role: worker,\n+\t\tPlanURL: fmt.Sprintf(\"https://github.com/%s/blob/main/.ard/%d/plan.md\", t.l.d.Repo, is.Number)})\n+}\n+\n // askApproval posts the one-per-lead-job \"ready for approval\" comment. It\n // changes no label and records no event.\n func (t *tick) askApproval(ctx context.Context, n int, jobID, worker string, rounds int) error {\ndiff --git a/internal/triage/loop.go b/internal/triage/loop.go\nindex 39910e2..0c09bbd 100644\n--- a/internal/triage/loop.go\n+++ b/internal/triage/loop.go\n@@ -101,6 +101,9 @@ type Deps struct {\n \t// entry at that SHA (no content). nil for either holds a network round.\n \tMainSHA   func(ctx context.Context) (string, error)\n \tMainEntry func(ctx context.Context, sha, path string) (TreeEntry, bool, error)\n+\t// Approvals, when set, lists the issues waiting for ard:approved so the\n+\t// command center can offer to approve them. nil = not tracked.\n+\tApprovals *ApprovalQueue\n }\n \n // Loop is the triage loop. It implements controller.Loop.\ndiff --git a/internal/triage/queue.go b/internal/triage/queue.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..23e0b04\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/triage/queue.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@\n+package triage\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"sort\"\n+\t\"sync\"\n+)\n+\n+// QueueItem is one issue waiting for a human to add ard:approved.\n+type QueueItem struct {\n+\tIssue   int\n+\tTitle   string\n+\tRole    string\n+\tPlanURL string\n+}\n+\n+// ApprovalQueue is the in-memory list of issues the gate is waiting on. The\n+// triage loop writes it; the command center reads it. Safe for concurrent use.\n+type ApprovalQueue struct {\n+\tmu    sync.Mutex\n+\titems map[int]QueueItem\n+}\n+\n+// Add records or refreshes an item; a repeat does not duplicate it.\n+func (q *ApprovalQueue) Add(it QueueItem) {\n+\tif q == nil {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tq.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer q.mu.Unlock()\n+\tif q.items == nil {\n+\t\tq.items = map[int]QueueItem{}\n+\t}\n+\tq.items[it.Issue] = it\n+}\n+\n+// Remove drops issue n.\n+func (q *ApprovalQueue) Remove(n int) {\n+\tif q == nil {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tq.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer q.mu.Unlock()\n+\tdelete(q.items, n)\n+}\n+\n+// Snapshot returns the items ordered by issue number.\n+func (q *ApprovalQueue) Snapshot() []QueueItem {\n+\tif q == nil {\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tq.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer q.mu.Unlock()\n+\tout := make([]QueueItem, 0, len(q.items))\n+\tfor _, it := range q.items {\n+\t\tout = append(out, it)\n+\t}\n+\tsort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].Issue < out[j].Issue })\n+\treturn out\n+}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012EkNRdyWKreWe2Ep9j3Dx1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
